<Project>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       THE CONSUMER RESOLUTION CONTRACT for FS.GG.Governance.ReferenceGateSet
       (FS-GG/FS.GG.Governance#386 AC2; docs/decisions/0011-generated-reference-gate-set.md).

       WHAT WAS BROKEN. This package publishes its payload under `contentFiles/any/any/`. A modern
       SDK-style `PackageReference` does NOT materialize `contentFiles` into the consumer's working
       tree — that is a `packages.config`/`PackageReference`-with-`contentFiles`-assets legacy — and
       the package shipped no `build`/`buildTransitive` targets either. So there was no verb at all
       by which an ordinary repository could OBTAIN the published profile; the only documented route
       was copying `samples/sdd-reference-gate-set/` by hand out of a clone of this repo, which is
       not a resolution of the PACKAGE and could not be pinned, verified, or re-resolved.

       WHAT THIS IS. One explicit, idempotent MSBuild target that copies the package's published
       `.fsgg/` into the consuming repository:

         dotnet restore
         dotnet msbuild -t:FsggResolveReferenceGateSet

       It is deliberately NOT hooked to `Build`, `Restore`, or any other event. Resolving writes
       files into the consumer's SOURCE tree, and a build that silently rewrites tracked files is a
       worse contract than a missing one. The consumer runs the verb when it wants the profile, and
       the write shows up in its diff where it can be reviewed.

       WHAT THIS IS NOT — and this is the load-bearing part. This is DISTRIBUTION, never
       ENFORCEMENT. ADR-0009 §Decision 1 rejected resolving the org floor from an installed package
       because a floor a product can escape by deleting a file is not a floor, and
       docs/decisions/0011 PRESERVES that rejection rather than overturning it. The enforced floor
       remains the embedded F# profile (`ReferenceProfile.checksFor`), which
       `Inheritance.applyInheritance` unions into every `game` product's gate set before
       `Ship.rollup` with no file read anywhere in the path. Deleting, editing, or never resolving
       the `.fsgg/` this target writes changes what a product DECLARES; it cannot change what the
       product INHERITS. That is why an escapable copy is safe here and would not have been safe as
       the enforcement input.

       Properties a consumer may set:

         FsggReferenceGateSetDestination   where to write. Default: `$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/.fsgg`.
                                           An ordinary repository usually wants its REPO ROOT, e.g.
                                           `-p:FsggReferenceGateSetDestination=$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/../.fsgg`.
         FsggReferenceGateSetOverwrite     `true` (default) re-resolves in place; `false` refuses to
                                           overwrite existing files so a local edit is never lost.

       Read-only properties this file publishes for a consumer's own gates:

         FsggReferenceGateSetSource          the package's `.fsgg/` directory.
         FsggReferenceGateSetSchemaManifest  the in-package `schema-manifest.json` (ADR-0055) — the
                                             four contained `schemaVersion` generations, so a
                                             consumer can pin against the schema generation rather
                                             than scraping the package version string.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- This file is imported from `<package-root>/buildTransitive/`, so the payload is one level
         up. NormalizeDirectory keeps the trailing slash and collapses the `..` so the value is a
         real path in diagnostics rather than a path with a `..` in the middle of it. -->
    <FsggReferenceGateSetPackageRoot>$([MSBuild]::NormalizeDirectory('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)', '..'))</FsggReferenceGateSetPackageRoot>
    <FsggReferenceGateSetSource>$([MSBuild]::NormalizeDirectory('$(FsggReferenceGateSetPackageRoot)', 'contentFiles', 'any', 'any', '.fsgg'))</FsggReferenceGateSetSource>
    <FsggReferenceGateSetSchemaManifest>$([MSBuild]::NormalizePath('$(FsggReferenceGateSetPackageRoot)', 'contentFiles', 'any', 'any', 'schema-manifest.json'))</FsggReferenceGateSetSchemaManifest>

    <FsggReferenceGateSetDestination Condition="'$(FsggReferenceGateSetDestination)' == ''">$([MSBuild]::NormalizeDirectory('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)', '.fsgg'))</FsggReferenceGateSetDestination>
    <FsggReferenceGateSetOverwrite Condition="'$(FsggReferenceGateSetOverwrite)' == ''">true</FsggReferenceGateSetOverwrite>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Resolve the published reference gate set into this repository's `.fsgg/`. -->
  <Target Name="FsggResolveReferenceGateSet">

    <ItemGroup>
      <FsggReferenceGateSetFile Include="$(FsggReferenceGateSetSource)**\*" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!-- Fail LOUD and CLOSED on an empty payload. A `Copy` of nothing succeeds, so without this the
         verb would report success and leave the consumer with no `.fsgg/` at all — the exact
         "resolved, apparently" failure this contract exists to remove. -->
    <Error Condition="'@(FsggReferenceGateSetFile)' == ''"
           Code="FSGG0386"
           Text="FS.GG.Governance.ReferenceGateSet: no files found under '$(FsggReferenceGateSetSource)'. The package payload is missing or the package layout changed; refusing to report a resolution that produced nothing." />

    <Copy SourceFiles="@(FsggReferenceGateSetFile)"
          DestinationFolder="$(FsggReferenceGateSetDestination)%(RecursiveDir)"
          SkipUnchangedFiles="false"
          Condition="'$(FsggReferenceGateSetOverwrite)' == 'true'" />

    <Copy SourceFiles="@(FsggReferenceGateSetFile)"
          DestinationFolder="$(FsggReferenceGateSetDestination)%(RecursiveDir)"
          SkipUnchangedFiles="false"
          Condition="'$(FsggReferenceGateSetOverwrite)' != 'true' And !Exists('$(FsggReferenceGateSetDestination)%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)')" />

    <Message Importance="high"
             Text="FS.GG.Governance.ReferenceGateSet: resolved @(FsggReferenceGateSetFile->Count()) file(s) into $(FsggReferenceGateSetDestination) (schema manifest: $(FsggReferenceGateSetSchemaManifest)). This is the DECLARED profile; the enforced floor stays embedded in the governance runtime (docs/decisions/0011, ADR-0009 §1)." />
  </Target>

</Project>
